          "**Brain growth**: the brain reaches about **80% of adult size by 2-3 years**, driven by dendritic branching, **synaptogenesis** (up to a million new synapses a second in infancy) and **myelination**, followed by experience-driven **synaptic pruning** - so the first 1000 days are the window of greatest gain and harm. [Nelson 22e]",
