          "**Dexamethasone 0.15-0.6 mg/kg orally as a single dose (maximum 16 mg)** is first line; **0.15 mg/kg is as effective as 0.6 mg/kg** for mild-moderate croup, and 0.6 mg/kg is used for severe croup; the IV tablet solution or crushed tablet can be mixed in a spoon of honey, jaggery water or juice. [Nelson 22e]",
          "If the child is **vomiting**, give **dexamethasone IM or IV at the same dose**, or **nebulised budesonide 2 mg** (as 2 mL of 0.5 mg/mL x 2, undiluted) as an alternative; **prednisolone 1 mg/kg orally** is acceptable where dexamethasone is unavailable but slightly less effective. [Nelson 22e]",
          "**Nebulised L-adrenaline 1:1000 (1 mg/mL), 0.5 mL/kg (maximum 5 mL) undiluted**, with oxygen, for moderate-severe croup or stridor at rest; **racemic adrenaline 2.25% 0.05 mL/kg (maximum 0.5 mL)** is equivalent; it may be repeated every 15-20 minutes in severe cases while arranging transfer. [Nelson 22e]",
